---

This section covers how user-defined Context Objects are passed around in
callbacks.

## Overview

The Context Object is passed to call callbacks and event handlers through the
`context` property. The purpose of the Context Object is to attach additional
information to custom callbacks such as [Formatters](./formatters/) and [Tooltip Renderers](./tooltips/#using-custom-tooltips).

## Context Object Overrides

The Context Object can be set using the `context` property either at the root of
the chart options, or on individual series and axes. The options
`series[].context` and `axes[].context` will be used for callbacks related to
the target series or axis, but will fallback to the root `context` property if
not set.

```js
{
    context: 'my root context',
    series: [
        {
            marker: {
                itemStyler: ({ context }) => {
                    console.log(context); // prints 'my root context'
                },
            },
        },
        {
            context: 'my series context',
            marker: {
                itemStyler: ({ context }) => {
                    console.log(context); // prints 'my series context'
                },
            },
        },
    ],
    axes: [
        {
            type: 'number',
            position: 'bottom',
            label: {
                formatter: ({ context }) => {
                    console.log(context); // prints 'my root context'
                },
            },
        },
        {
            type: 'number',
            position: 'left',
            context: 'my axis context',
            label: {
                formatter: ({ context }) => {
                    console.log(context); // prints 'my axis context'
                },
            },
        },
    ],
};
```

In this example:

-   `series[0]` and `axes[0]` do not have the `context` defined, so the
    callbacks use the `context` defined at the root.

-   `series[1]` and `axes[1]` have custom `context` values defined, which is
    what is used in the callbacks.

## Context Object Example

The example below shows how the Context Object can be used.

Changing the User Currency in the dropdown updates the Context Object
state. Note that the Context Object is used by the following callbacks:

-   The Y-axis Label Formatter, to convert USD values to the preferred User Currency.

-   The Tooltip Renderer, to render both the stock prices in USD and the User
    Currency (if applicable).

-   The Context Menu Actions, to log converted stock prices in the console.

